<title>USA: U.S. Gulf rigs under contract up 1 at 160.</title>
<headline>U.S. Gulf rigs under contract up 1 at 160.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 160 rigs under contract in the U.S. Gulf as of January 10, up one from the period ending January 3, Offshore Data Services said Friday.</p>
<p>The utilization rate for rigs working in the Gulf, based on a total fleet of 181, was 88.4 percent.</p>
<p>The number of working rigs in the European/Mediterranean area remained the same this week at 106 rigs under contract out of a total fleet of 107, a utilization rate of  99.1 pct.</p>
<p>The worldwide rig count rose one to 557 out of a total fleet of 606, making the utilization rate 91.9 percent.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk 212-859-1620</p>
</text>
